# No agent watch loops

Do **not** burn tokens on tight `--watch` / sleep-poll loops for bot gates. GitHub Actions and squash auto-merge already own that wait. This does **not** mean hand work back to the user.

## Forbidden busy-poll patterns

```sh
npm run wait-for-bots -- --watch
npm run pr:gates:check -- --watch
gh pr checks <n> --watch
while true; do npm run wait-for-bots; sleep 45; done
```

## Required ownership

```sh
npm run pr:arm-and-park -- --pr <n>
```

| Exit | Action |
|------|--------|
| 0 | Ready — finish any post-merge steps you still own |
| 2 | Waiting on bots/CI only — auto-merge armed; **keep ownership** via self-wake (`/loop`, heartbeat, or next-turn re-check). Do **not** tell the user to follow up. |
| 3 | Actionable — fix, push, re-run arm-and-park |
| 1 | Error — diagnose and fix |

Waiting is fine. Abandoning the loop to the user is not. See global rule `own-followthrough-never-handoff`.
